            <ArticleTitle>[A rare cause of 2:1 atrioventricular block and congestive heart failure in preterm infants: Hypocalcemia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>82-84</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5543/tkda.2016.82453</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Atrioventricular (AV) block in the neonatal period is a rare disorder. It is frequently associated with underlying structural congenital heart disease and maternal lupus. Presently described is premature baby who developed 2:1 AV block and congestive heart failure due to hypocalcemia. Dramatic clinical improvement was observed following treatment of intravenous 10% calcium gluconate. Therefore, it is suggested that serum calcium level of newborns with AV block and congestive heart failure be measured.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
